.TH "CSSNUMERICARRAY.LENGTH" "3JS" "August 15, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSNumericArray.length \- CSSNumericArray: length property
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]length\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]CSSNumericArray\f[R] interface returns the number of items in the
object.
.SH VALUE
An integer.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
In this example, we read the \f[CR]length\f[R] of the
\f[CR]CSSNumericArray\f[R] returned by the \f[CR]values\f[R] property of
a \f[CR]CSSMathSum\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] sum = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSMathSum(CSS.px(10), CSS.em(5), CSS.percent(50));

console.log(sum.values.length); \f[I]// 3\f[R]
.EE
